! This is "TCD_15sOP", a 15 node (species) compact kinetic model for the combustion of methane in air.
! Created on 22/6/2021 using MLOCK1.0 - a Coded Algorithm for Machine Learned Optimisation of Chemical Kinetics [1,2].
! TCD_15sOP is optimised to replicate the calculations of NUIGMECH1.0 [2].

! Units are cm, s, mol, cal.
! Validated to PSR calculations at performance targets of Phi (in air) 0.4-1.5, 1000 - 2000K, 1 - 40 Atm.
! Validated to constant UV homogeneous reactor (IDT) calculations at phi (fuel in air) 0.4-1.5, 1100 - 2000K, 1 - 40 Atm.
! Validated to freely propagating flame calculations at phi (fuel in air) 0.4-1.5, 473-673K, 1 - 40 Atm.
! Model Fidelity to these validation targets can be found at [1,4]
!
! Authors: Mark Kelly (1), Mark Fortune (1), Gilles Bourque (2,3), Stephen Dooley (1)
! Affiliations: (1) School of Physics, Trinity College Dublin, Dublin, Ireland
!               (2) Siemens Energy Canada Ltd, Montréal, QC H9P 1A5, Canada
!               (3) McGill University, Montréal, QC H9P 1A5, Canada
!
! Sponsorship: Siemens Energy Canada Ltd, Sustainable Energy and Fuel Efficiency (SEFE) Spoke of MaREI (16/SP/3829), Irish Research Council (GOIPG/2020/1043)
! Contact: Kellym67@tcd.ie or stephen.dooley@tcd.ie.
!
!References:
![1] TBC
![2] Kelly M,  Bourque G, Dooley S,  ASME Turbo Expo 2021: Turbomachinery Technical Conference and Exposition 2021.
![3] Baigmohammadi M, Patel V, Martinez S, Panigrahy S, Ramalingam A, Burke U, et al. Energy & Fuels. 2020; 34:3755-71
![4] https://www.tcd.ie/Physics/research/groups/energy-science-low-carbon/models/
!

!\START_ELEMENTS_LIST
ELEMENTS
C
H
